module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionFullyFaithful.PrincipalComplete
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.FormalSections

/-!
# The two spellings of the principal ideal sheaf on the complement

Let `A` be a commutative ring, let `𝔞 ⊆ A` be an ideal, let `f ∈ A` and let
`U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`. The ideal sheaf `f 𝒪_U` is written in two ways in this library:

* `Stacks.Algebraization.complementPrincipalIdealSheaf A 𝔞 f`, the ideal sheaf generated by the
  single global function `Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementTopScalars 𝔞 f`, which is the spelling
  the statement of Stacks 0EKS uses;
* `Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A (Ideal.span {f}) 𝔞`, the extension to `U` of
  the ideal `(f) ⊆ A` along `U ⟶ Spec(A)`, which is the spelling the formal-sections material of
  Stacks 0EG2 and the closed subscheme `U ∩ V(f)` use.

This file identifies them.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.complementPrincipalIdealSheaf_eq_idealSheafNearVanishing` — the two
  spellings of `f 𝒪_U` agree.

## Implementation notes

Both sides are `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop` of an ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`,
so the statement reduces to an equality of ideals there. The structure map
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementTopScalars` and the one
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal` is defined from are the same ring homomorphism
`A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`, namely `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso` followed by the open immersion on
global functions; so the ideal on the second side is the image of `(f)`, and the image of a
principal ideal is principal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EG2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EG2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

open Stacks.LocalCohomology

/-- **The two spellings of the ideal sheaf `f 𝒪_U` on `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` agree.** The ideal
sheaf generated by the global function `f|_U` is the extension to `U` of the ideal `(f)` of `A`.

Both sides are generated by a single ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`, and those ideals are the image of
`(f)` under one and the same ring homomorphism `A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`. -/
public theorem complementPrincipalIdealSheaf_eq_idealSheafNearVanishing
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (a : Ideal A) (f : A) :
    complementPrincipalIdealSheaf A a f = idealSheafNearVanishing A (Ideal.span {f}) a := by
  have hideal : Ideal.span {complementTopScalars a f} =
      Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal A (Ideal.span {f})
        (complementZeroLocus A a).ι := by
    rw [Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  exact congrArg Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop hideal

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
